1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:11,175
Before touching any system, testers study what the organisation has already made public, like a consultant walking round the outside of a bank branch.

2
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:19,705
Websites, job adverts, public certificates and code can reveal forgotten systems and leaked keys.

3
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:30,700
Mature organisations run this research on themselves, all the time: new certificates, DNS changes and leaked keys.

4
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:35,400
They find forgotten systems before attackers do.

5
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:44,975
Only research the organisation that authorised you. Never use leaked passwords, and never trick staff.

6
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:50,895
Turn each finding into a fix, like revoking a leaked key at once.

